### Variables — fill in @token after running Login
@base = http://localhost:5112
@token = <paste_token_here>

### 1. Login (get token)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "YourPassword123!"
}

### 2. GET queue — all NeedsReview tickets
GET {{base}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. GET ticket detail
GET {{base}}/api/tickets/b1b2c3d4-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. PATCH draft — save edited reply
PATCH {{base}}/api/tickets/b1b2c3d4-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/draft
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "finalReply": "Dear Alice, we have resolved your login issue. Please try logging in now."
}

### 5. POST send — mark ticket as Sent
POST {{base}}/api/tickets/b1b2c3d4-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/send
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. GET queue again — ticket above should be gone (Sent)
GET {{base}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. GET sent ticket — status should be Sent
GET {{base}}/api/tickets/b1b2c3d4-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. POST send again — should return 409 Conflict
POST {{base}}/api/tickets/b1b2c3d4-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/send
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. GET unknown ticket — should return 404
GET {{base}}/api/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. No token — should return 401
GET {{base}}/api/tickets
